WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.660 --> 00:00:01.920
- [Narrator] This man rubbing shoulders

00:00:01.920 --> 00:00:04.170
with the likes of Natalie
Portman, Paul McCartney

00:00:04.170 --> 00:00:08.010
and Rihanna is French business
mogul Bernard Arnault.

00:00:08.010 --> 00:00:10.260
While he might not be as
recognizable as those three,

00:00:10.260 --> 00:00:12.960
he's got more money than
all of them combined.

00:00:12.960 --> 00:00:15.120
Arnault is the world's richest person

00:00:15.120 --> 00:00:19.890
with a net worth of $191
billion at the start of 2023.

00:00:19.890 --> 00:00:22.740
- He is one of the most important
businessmen in the world,

00:00:22.740 --> 00:00:25.410
certainly the most important
in France right now.

00:00:25.410 --> 00:00:26.250
- [Narrator] He is the CEO

00:00:26.250 --> 00:00:28.740
of LVMH Moët Hennessy Louis Vuitton,

00:00:28.740 --> 00:00:30.960
which is basically the
first word in luxury.

00:00:30.960 --> 00:00:32.760
In addition to Louis
Vuitton, the conglomerate

00:00:32.760 --> 00:00:35.250
includes brands such as Dior, Tiffany's,

00:00:35.250 --> 00:00:36.750
and Belvedere Vodka.

00:00:36.750 --> 00:00:41.750
- Luxury for for me is
how can you create desire?

00:00:42.510 --> 00:00:45.060
- [Narrator] He's been in
charge of LVMH since 1989

00:00:45.060 --> 00:00:45.930
and all of his children

00:00:45.930 --> 00:00:48.420
have powerful roles within the business.

00:00:48.420 --> 00:00:50.640
Here's Bernard Arnault built his wealth

00:00:50.640 --> 00:00:53.600
and how he plans to keep
it under family control.

00:00:53.600 --> 00:00:56.130
(playful music)
(paparazzi chatting)

00:00:56.130 --> 00:00:58.440
The richest person in the
world isn't a tabloid mainstay

00:00:58.440 --> 00:00:59.760
or red carpet regular,

00:00:59.760 --> 00:01:01.200
even if he is seen on the front row

00:01:01.200 --> 00:01:02.790
at his brands' fashion shows.

00:01:02.790 --> 00:01:06.240
- He's a guy who is somewhat shy.

00:01:06.240 --> 00:01:08.610
He's even maybe a tiny bit awkward.

00:01:08.610 --> 00:01:11.550
There's a saying, which gets
repeated to me constantly

00:01:11.550 --> 00:01:15.545
by French billionaires
and French CEOs, which is

00:01:15.545 --> 00:01:17.130
(Nick speaking in French)

00:01:17.130 --> 00:01:19.350
which basically means to live happily,

00:01:19.350 --> 00:01:20.640
you have to live hidden.

00:01:20.640 --> 00:01:22.410
- [Narrator] The beginning
of the Arnault empire starts

00:01:22.410 --> 00:01:24.300
with an acquisition, which
would become something

00:01:24.300 --> 00:01:27.150
of a modus operandi for
him over the next 30 years.

00:01:27.150 --> 00:01:30.480
In 1984, he took over
Boussac, the holding company

00:01:30.480 --> 00:01:33.000
that owned French fashion
house Christian Dior.

00:01:33.000 --> 00:01:36.720
- Christian Dior is maybe
the most recognizable

00:01:36.720 --> 00:01:39.840
and the most well-known
fashion name in the world.

00:01:39.840 --> 00:01:40.830
- [Narrator] He sold off pretty much all

00:01:40.830 --> 00:01:42.330
of the group's brands but Dior,

00:01:42.330 --> 00:01:43.930
and pulled it out of bankruptcy.

00:01:44.880 --> 00:01:45.713
In the late '80s,

00:01:45.713 --> 00:01:47.940
Dior's revival helped
Arnault a massive stake

00:01:47.940 --> 00:01:49.920
in the recently founded LVMH,

00:01:49.920 --> 00:01:52.200
of which he soon became
the majority shareholder,

00:01:52.200 --> 00:01:54.480
CEO and chairman.

00:01:54.480 --> 00:01:57.090
Over 30 years and several
acquisitions later,

00:01:57.090 --> 00:01:59.280
LVMH now includes 75 brands,

00:01:59.280 --> 00:02:02.103
covering wine, jewelry,
hotels and fashion.

00:02:02.940 --> 00:02:04.950
The European company has also expanded

00:02:04.950 --> 00:02:07.650
into China and the US
where Arnault once joined

00:02:07.650 --> 00:02:09.780
then President Donald Trump at the opening

00:02:09.780 --> 00:02:12.060
of a Louis Vuitton factory in Texas.

00:02:12.060 --> 00:02:14.010
- He's a great gentleman,
a great businessman

00:02:14.010 --> 00:02:15.900
and he's really an artist.

00:02:15.900 --> 00:02:17.340
To me, Bernard is an artist

00:02:17.340 --> 00:02:19.770
and what he's done is incredible.

00:02:19.770 --> 00:02:20.700
- [Narrator] The luxury giant now

00:02:20.700 --> 00:02:23.940
has a market value of nearly $438 billion

00:02:23.940 --> 00:02:26.463
and revenue last year
was around $86 billion.

00:02:27.330 --> 00:02:29.520
These results have
boosted Arnault's wealth

00:02:29.520 --> 00:02:30.450
and put him above the likes

00:02:30.450 --> 00:02:33.990
of big tech billionaires such
as Elon Musk and Jeff Bezos.

00:02:33.990 --> 00:02:35.940
While those men have seen
their company shares drop

00:02:35.940 --> 00:02:38.280
in recent months, LVMH's share price

00:02:38.280 --> 00:02:43.260
is up over 165% since
lows in March of 2020.

00:02:43.260 --> 00:02:44.190
Though the stock market

00:02:44.190 --> 00:02:46.952
is apparently not something
Arnault pays attention to.

00:02:46.952 --> 00:02:50.790
(Bernard speaking in French)

00:02:50.790 --> 00:02:52.470
- [Narrator] That price
boost was thanks to a surge

00:02:52.470 --> 00:02:54.630
and demand for luxury
goods during the pandemic

00:02:54.630 --> 00:02:57.690
when affluent shoppers were
stuck at home flush with cash.

00:02:57.690 --> 00:02:59.370
And more recently, China's loosening

00:02:59.370 --> 00:03:01.470
of strict COVID-19 rules.

00:03:01.470 --> 00:03:04.950
The country is one of the luxury
industry's biggest markets.

00:03:04.950 --> 00:03:08.040
- Bernard Arnault himself
has a ton of legitimacy

00:03:08.040 --> 00:03:10.200
because he built up this
company from scratch.

00:03:10.200 --> 00:03:13.230
He built this empire
through several battles.

00:03:13.230 --> 00:03:14.520
He's obviously involved

00:03:14.520 --> 00:03:17.190
in all the key aspects of the business.

00:03:17.190 --> 00:03:19.320
- [Narrator] Also involved in
key aspects of the business

00:03:19.320 --> 00:03:21.240
are his five children who are often seen

00:03:21.240 --> 00:03:22.920
with him at brand events.

00:03:22.920 --> 00:03:24.033
Let's meet the family.

00:03:25.260 --> 00:03:28.350
Arnault married his first
wife, Anne Dewavrin, in 1973

00:03:28.350 --> 00:03:30.750
and they had two children,
Delphine and Antoine.

00:03:31.770 --> 00:03:34.470
Delphine is the newly minted
CEO of Christian Dior,

00:03:34.470 --> 00:03:35.850
while her younger brother, Antoine,

00:03:35.850 --> 00:03:37.803
is CEO of the family holding company.

00:03:39.150 --> 00:03:41.910
After divorcing Anne, Arnault
married Helene Mercier

00:03:41.910 --> 00:03:43.830
and had three more children.

00:03:43.830 --> 00:03:45.900
Alexandre holds an executive
vice president position

00:03:45.900 --> 00:03:49.560
at Tiffany's, the American
jeweler LVMH took over in 2021.

00:03:49.560 --> 00:03:52.770
Frederic is CEO of watchmaker Tag Heuer,

00:03:52.770 --> 00:03:54.540
and Jean heads up marketing development

00:03:54.540 --> 00:03:55.840
for Louis Vuitton watches.

00:03:57.343 --> 00:04:01.093
(Bernard speaking in French)

00:04:06.570 --> 00:04:08.460
- [Narrator] The Arnaults
own more than 97% of Dior,

00:04:08.460 --> 00:04:10.713
which in turn owns 41% of LVMH.

00:04:11.580 --> 00:04:15.270
The family also owns close
to 7% of LVMH directly.

00:04:15.270 --> 00:04:16.290
On top of that,

00:04:16.290 --> 00:04:19.080
they have total voting
rights of more than 60%.

00:04:19.080 --> 00:04:21.480
- So essentially what the Arnaults

00:04:21.480 --> 00:04:23.400
and what Bernard Arnault himself decides

00:04:23.400 --> 00:04:24.930
goes in that company.

00:04:24.930 --> 00:04:26.370
- [Narrator] And Arnault has taken steps

00:04:26.370 --> 00:04:29.250
to ensure his family retains
control over the empire.

00:04:29.250 --> 00:04:33.030
Last year, LVMH voted to raise
the age limit of its CEO,

00:04:33.030 --> 00:04:35.220
meaning the 73-year-old
Arnault could remain

00:04:35.220 --> 00:04:37.680
in charge until he's 80, if he wishes.

00:04:37.680 --> 00:04:40.380
He also changed the structure
of the family holding company.

00:04:40.380 --> 00:04:43.770
- The children will each have
a 20% stake in this structure

00:04:43.770 --> 00:04:46.920
and they can't sell
their shares for 30 years

00:04:46.920 --> 00:04:48.480
and it essentially will keep the shares

00:04:48.480 --> 00:04:50.160
in the family even beyond that.

00:04:50.160 --> 00:04:51.660
And it's one of the kind

00:04:51.660 --> 00:04:54.210
of favorite pastimes in
Parisian business circle

00:04:54.210 --> 00:04:56.370
to kind of watch his children

00:04:56.370 --> 00:04:59.190
and track their progress
with a view to succession.

00:04:59.190 --> 00:05:01.350
- [Narrator] Arnault has not
publicly named a successor

00:05:01.350 --> 00:05:02.820
but whoever it is will inherit a company

00:05:02.820 --> 00:05:04.860
that has successfully
navigated the pandemic

00:05:04.860 --> 00:05:07.230
amid concerns for the
future of the industry.

00:05:07.230 --> 00:05:08.910
High inflation and the war in Ukraine

00:05:08.910 --> 00:05:10.320
have prompted estimates of a slowdown

00:05:10.320 --> 00:05:12.870
in luxury good sales in 2023.

00:05:12.870 --> 00:05:14.310
And in China, a recent wave

00:05:14.310 --> 00:05:17.730
of COVID infections means
life there remains disrupted.

00:05:17.730 --> 00:05:20.520
Economists also haven't
ruled out a global recession.

00:05:20.520 --> 00:05:21.720
For now though at least,

00:05:21.720 --> 00:05:24.210
the luxury market's wealthy
customers seem happy

00:05:24.210 --> 00:05:25.560
to keep spending.

00:05:25.560 --> 00:05:26.880
- The luxury goods industry

00:05:26.880 --> 00:05:28.440
has been a good one for investors

00:05:28.440 --> 00:05:33.030
in part because global
wealth every year is rising.

00:05:33.030 --> 00:05:34.710
And so more and more people are coming

00:05:34.710 --> 00:05:36.810
into the luxury goods market each year

00:05:36.810 --> 00:05:40.047
and that's obviously good for
LVMH, for Bernard Arnault,

00:05:40.047 --> 00:05:42.615
and for people selling luxury goods.

00:05:42.615 --> 00:05:45.282
(playful music)

